  "id": "Compound::DB00622 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Nicardipine is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of Cyp2c19 in the arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities, both of which are catalyzed by Cyp2c8. These pathways are central to the metabolism of arachidonic acid, which plays a role in inflammatory and vascular processes. The evidence suggests a direct interaction between Nicardipine and Cyp2c8 through a chain of enzymatic activities involving Cyp2c19. The scores from the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Nicardipine influences Cyp2c8 remains partially inferred. The presence of multiple overlapping pathways involving Cyp2c19 and Cyp2c8 supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Nicardipine in modulating Cyp2c8 activity.",
